Perfect! I found the issue! Looking at lines 167-182 of `streaming_contracts.py`, the `to_bytes()` method correctly builds an error chunk with the `error` field:

```python
if self.is_done:
    # Check for error metadata first
    if (
        self.metadata.get("finish_reason") == "error"
        and "error" in self.metadata
    ):
        error_data = {
            "choices": [{"delta": {}, "finish_reason": "error"}],
            "error": self.metadata["error"],
        }
        ...
        return f"data: {json.dumps(error_data)}\n\ndata: [DONE]\n\n".encode()
```

